  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given an array A=[A1,A2,…,AN]A = [A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_N]A=[A1​,A2​,…,AN​] of length NNN, containing **positive** integers.\n\nAn index iii is said to be cursed if A1+A2+…+Ai−1≥AiA_1 + A_2 + \\ldots + A_{i - 1} \\ge A_iA1​+A2​+…+Ai−1​≥Ai​.\n\nIn particular, Ai≥1A_i\\geq 1Ai​≥1 means that index 111 is always **not** cursed.\n\nYou can rearrange AAA as you wish to. Find the minimum possible number of cursed indices in the rearranged array.\n\nAlso find any rearrangement that achieves this minimum.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN, the size of the array.\nThe next line contains NNN space-separated integers, A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output two lines.\n\n\n\nThe first line should contain a single integer, the minimum number of cursed indices after rearranging array AAA as you like.\nThe second line should contain NNN space-separated integers representing a rearrangement of AAA that attains this minimum number of cursed indices.\n\nIf there are multiple rearrangements that attain the minimum, you may print **any** of them.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤2⋅1041 \\leq T \\leq 2\\cdot 10^41≤T≤2⋅104",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 10510^5105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n3\n1 1 1\n3\n4 2 1\n2\n6 5\n3\n1 2 3",
        "output": "2\n1 1 1\n0\n1 2 4\n0\n5 6\n1\n1 2 3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: [1,1,1][1, 1, 1][1,1,1] is the only possible rearrangement, and has 222 cursed indices:\n\nA1=1≥A2=1A_1 = 1 \\ge A_2 = 1A1​=1≥A2​=1, so index 222 is cursed.\nA1+A2=2≥A3=1A_1 + A_2 = 2 \\ge A_3 = 1A1​+A2​=2≥A3​=1, so index 333 is cursed.\n\nTest case 222: The rearrangement of the array AAA to [1,2,4][1, 2, 4][1,2,4] has no cursed indices.\nTest case 333: The rearrangement [5,6][5, 6][5,6] has no cursed indices.\nTest case 444: The optimal rearrangement is [1,2,3][1, 2, 3][1,2,3], and it has 111 cursed index: A1+A2=3≥A3=3A_1 + A_2 = 3 \\ge A_3 = 3A1​+A2​=3≥A3​=3 so index 333 is cursed."
      }
    ]
  },
